1 Mardu W/B/R, 3 Orzhov W/B, 5 Boros W/R, 3 Rakdos B/R, 3 Mono-White, 3 Mono-Black, 5 Mono-Red. The cheapest one with a real list is <strong>These New Cards Work So Well in Mono White Enchantments | Standard BO1 MTGA Gameplay #mtgarena</strong> (Mono-White) by AbojiiMTG at $93.06 paper and 14 rare-plus-mythic wildcards.</p>

<div class="note">
<strong>"Mardu" means the full W/B/R three-color build, nothing less.</strong> A mono-white deck is a mono-white deck.
An Orzhov deck is white-black. A Boros deck is white-red. A Rakdos deck is black-red. Those all happen to run on the
same mana base you already own, so they are worth listing, and the badge on each row names what the deck actually is
rather than filing all seven combinations under one word. The seven color combinations that fit are
W, B, R, W/B, W/R, B/R, and W/B/R.
</div>
<div class="note">
